  "the machine caught": "机器抓到了",
  "Not once — not because you were careless, but because the change was smaller than an eye can catch in that time. That is not your fault. That is why this job should not sit with one pair of eyes.": "一次都没抓到——不是因为你粗心，而是因为变化小到眼睛在那段时间里抓不住。这不是你的错。所以这份工作不该只靠一双眼睛。",
  "You missed most of them, which is what a human eye is built for over short stretches. The machine is not cleverer — it is just never bored.": "你漏掉了大多数。人眼在短时间里就是这样。机器并不更聪明——它只是永远不会无聊。",
  "You did better than most people do on this drill. Notice how you knew: heard it, saw it, or guessed. That answer is not the one the next person will give.": "你在这次练习里比大多数人做得好。留意你是怎么知道的：听到的、看到的，还是猜的。下一个人不会给出同一个答案。",
  "Six still screens. You will find out what you miss yourself, before anyone argues about who should be watching.": "六块静止的屏幕。在任何人争论该由谁来看之前，你会先知道自己漏掉了什么。",
  "Practice first — one screen will flash, clearly, then go dark. Press the one that flashed.": "先练习——会有一块屏幕清楚地闪一下，然后变暗。按下闪过的那一块。",
